.TH SHOWCMM 1 "August 2026" "showcmm" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
showcmm \- Shell command usage tracker and analyzer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B showcmm
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B showcmm
is a command-line tool for tracking, analyzing, and understanding shell command usage.

It imports shell history, stores command statistics locally in SQLite, and provides
commands for viewing and filtering command usage.

.B showcmm
also provides optional AI-powered analysis for evaluating command-line habits,
suggesting improvements, analyzing workflows, and generating useful aliases.

.SH COMMANDS

.TP
.B view
View command usage statistics.

.TP
.B update
Import shell history into the command database.

.TP
.B delete
Delete the local command history database.

.TP
.B ai
Analyze command-line habits using an AI model.

.SH VIEW OPTIONS

.TP
.B \-t, \-\-top
Show the most frequently used commands.

.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Show all tracked commands.

.TP
.B \-f, \-\-filter \fIQUERY\fR
Show commands matching the specified query.

.TP
.B \-l, \-\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit the number of commands displayed.
The default is 10.

.SH AI OPTIONS

The
.B ai
command supports several analysis modes.

.TP
.B \-\-roast
Roast your command-line habits based on your command usage.

.TP
.B \-\-learn
Suggest areas, tools, or concepts that may be useful to learn.

.TP
.B \-\-workflow
Analyze command usage and suggest workflow improvements.

.TP
.B \-\-level
Assess your command-line skill level.

.TP
.B \-\-alias
Suggest useful shell aliases based on command usage.

.SH CONFIGURATION

Shell configuration is stored in:

.EX
~/.config/showcmm/config.toml
.EE

The configuration defines the shell history file and parser used to process it.

Example:

.EX
[shells.bash]
path = "~/.bash_history"
parser = "plain"

[shells.zsh]
path = "~/.zsh_history"
parser = "zsh"

[shells.fish]
path = "~/.local/share/fish/fish_history"
parser = "fish"
.EE

Supported parsers currently include
.B plain,
.B zsh,
and
.B fish.

Additional parsers can be implemented in the project's
.B utils/parser.py
module.

.SH AI CONFIGURATION

AI provider, model, and prompts are configured in
.B config.py.

By default,
.B showcmm
uses OpenRouter's free model routing:

.EX
MODEL = "openrouter/free"
BASE_URL = "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1"
.EE

The model and API endpoint can be changed to another OpenAI-compatible
provider.

An external provider API key can be supplied through a
.B .env
file:

.EX
API_KEY=your_api_key
.EE

.B showcmm
can also be configured to use a local model if the local inference server
provides an OpenAI-compatible API.

.SH PRIVACY

Shell history is processed locally and stored in a local SQLite database.

For AI analysis, command history is normalized and aggregated into command
frequency statistics before being sent to an external AI provider.

Raw shell history and individual command arguments are not sent as part of
the AI analysis.

Local AI models can be used to keep AI processing on the user's machine.

.SH EXAMPLES

.TP
.B showcmm view
Show the top 10 commands.

.TP
.B showcmm view --top --limit 20
Show the 20 most frequently used commands.

.TP
.B showcmm view --all
Show all tracked commands.

.TP
.B showcmm view --filter git
Show commands containing "git".

.TP
.B showcmm update
Import shell history.

.TP
.B showcmm delete
Delete the tracked command history.

.TP
.B showcmm ai --roast
Roast your command-line habits.

.TP
.B showcmm ai --learn
Get suggestions for things to learn.

.TP
.B showcmm ai --workflow
Get suggestions for improving command-line workflows.

.TP
.B showcmm ai --level
Get an assessment of your command-line skill level.

.TP
.B showcmm ai --alias
Get suggestions for useful shell aliases.

.SH FILES

.TP
.I ~/.config/showcmm/config.toml
Shell history configuration.

.TP
.I commands.db
Local SQLite database containing command statistics.

.TP
.I .env
Optional API key configuration for external AI providers.

